WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.219 --> 00:00:03.200
-My first guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated actor,

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.701
a "New York Times"
best-selling author,

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:08.000
and a very, very,
very funny comedian.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.968
He now stars in the television
series "The Moodys."

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:12.534
And you can see
the second season

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:15.434
Thursday nights at 9:30 on Fox.

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:18.801
Here is Denis Leary!

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:20.834
Oh, that's what
I'm talking about!

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:22.434
Yes!
-Hey, pal.

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:25.334
-Oh, I wish you were here,
buddy. Oh, my gosh.

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:27.033
-Oh, I know. You know what?

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:28.434
The first thing
I was going to say

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:30.033
is I just --
I can't believe I'm not there.

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:32.200
But listen,
I'm half vaxxed, okay?

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.567
-Good.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:34.968
-I'm going to be fully vaxxed.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:37.033
Half vaxxed is pretty much
what a lot of people probably

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:38.701
say about me
and how I do things.

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:40.167
But I'm half vaxxed.

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:41.767
I'll be fully vaxxed
in two weeks.

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:44.100
So, then, you know,
hopefully I'll be able

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.367
to come into the studio
and see you.

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:47.667
It's so weird not to be live,
you know?

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:51.601
-But we have like over 50 people
in the audience now.

00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:53.033
So we actually have --
-That's what I heard.

00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:54.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:57.167
So we're so happy
that you can even do this.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:01:01.801
I know you're a big sports fan,
big Boston sports fan.

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:04.701
And I wanted to ask you about
Tom Brady

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:07.334
and how you felt,
him leaving the Patriots

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:10.834
and went on to win
the Super Bowl for Tampa Bay.

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:12.834
I know. Sorry to bring this up.

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:16.901
-So, listen. Sadly,
my plan didn't work out.

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:19.901
My plan was that Tom was going
to go to another team,

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:23.033
in this case, Tampa Bay,
and that team would suck,

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:24.167
and then he would come back.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:26.567
So it didn't really work out,
my plan.

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:28.000
-No.
-So I was shocked,

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.467
'cause I'm like,

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:32.467
he's going to a team that has
pewter-colored football pants.

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:36.067
I mean, literally, pewter
is the color of their pants.

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:38.467
-Pewter. Oh, my gosh.
-I mean, his wife's --

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:39.968
His wife's a fashion model.

00:01:39.968 --> 00:01:42.501
She must have said, "Honey, you
can't wear pewter-colored pants.

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:44.000
You can't."
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.634
-I couldn't be happier
that he won again.

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:49.534
And if there's any question
about him being

00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:52.501
the greatest of all time now,
that's seven Super Bowls, right?

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:54.868
-Yeah.
-And you'd have to get

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:58.000
all of the other multiple Super
Bowl-winning quarterbacks --

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.567
There's very few --
And if they want to prove

00:02:00.567 --> 00:02:02.100
they're the greatest
of all time,

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.334
throw the Lombardi Trophy
while you're drunk

00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:06.801
from one boat to another boat.

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:08.834
-That's the ultimate --
-That's the test.

00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:10.734
-That's exactly right.

00:02:10.734 --> 00:02:13.200
That's exactly right.
-That's the test.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:17.200
-I want to talk about this.
You do this every year,

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.300
this show called
"Comics Come Home"

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:20.701
in Boston.
-Yes.

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:23.334
-And I'm lucky enough to be
involved with it whenever I can,

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:26.801
whenever -- Every year
I've been going whenever I can.

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:29.834
It benefits
Cam Neely Foundation.

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:33.901
And we perform. I do stand-up,
or I make you sing a song.

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:35.400
-Yeah.
-And I got this footage

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.467
I wanted to show you,
because do you remember

00:02:37.467 --> 00:02:39.534
when you surprised me?
-Okay, wait, wait, wait.

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:41.400
Is this footage
from the John Mayer thing?

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.400
-Yeah.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.601
-Okay, you have to
let me set it up.

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:44.868
I love when Jimmy comes,

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:47.367
because we end up singing
a song together, you know?

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.167
Which is a blast.

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:51.667
So, I call John Mayer
without telling Jimmy.

00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:53.501
And I say, "Listen,
I have an idea.

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:55.601
You come on the show.
You play --

00:02:55.601 --> 00:02:57.200
Jimmy wants to do
'Walk This Way.'

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:00.167
You play 'Walk This Way,' but
we don't tell Jimmy in advance.

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:01.934
So Jimmy doesn't find out

00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:04.434
until you walk onstage
during the song.

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:07.000
Like, you'll start the riff.
[ Vocalizing "Walk This Way" ]

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.400
Offstage."
[ Vocalizing ]

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:10.667
You and I start singing.

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:13.367
Now, for people who have
never sung that song,

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:15.467
that's an incredibly
difficult song to sing,

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:18.767
not because of the, you know,
the level of the notes.

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:20.968
It's because the lyrics
are jam-packed,

00:03:20.968 --> 00:03:23.000
and they're unbelievably fast.
Right?

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.200
-Yeah.
-So Jimmy and I had rehearsed it

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.334
as trading lines back and forth.

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:30.767
So, you know, if one guy
misses a line,

00:03:30.767 --> 00:03:32.400
you're kind of screwed, right?

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.801
Jimmy comes out.

00:03:33.801 --> 00:03:36.400
[ Vocalizing "Walk This Way" ]

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.868
And me and Jimmy
start doing the song.

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:40.534
John Mayer walks out onstage.

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:43.000
The crowd goes nuts,
which they're supposed to.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.434
And Jimmy stopped singing.

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:46.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:48.367
Completely.

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:50.901
I figured he'd look
at John Mayer and be surprised.

00:03:50.901 --> 00:03:52.567
He looks at John Mayer
like he's surprised

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:55.000
and then goes over
and starts hugging John Mayer

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.300
and, like, hanging out with him.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:59.167
I'm like -- I'm singing
the entire song by myself.

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:02.033
[ Laughter ]
For like two verses.

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:03.467
-No -- Really?

00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:04.801
-Yeah.
-I don't remember that --

00:04:04.801 --> 00:04:06.567
But I just wanted
to show you a clip.

00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:08.133
I didn't know --
I forgot that I did that.

00:04:08.133 --> 00:04:10.767
Here's, I guess, the moment
where I spot John Mayer

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:12.934
surprising me at "Comics
Come Home" with Denis Leary.

00:04:12.934 --> 00:04:14.000
Take a look.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:19.467
♪♪

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:23.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:24.834
[ Laughter ]
-I was like, "Hey!"

00:04:24.834 --> 00:04:26.501
-You can hear me singing
in the background.

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:28.767
-I knew the guitar sounded good,
and your band is always great,

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:30.267
but I was like,
"That guitar sounds great."

00:04:30.267 --> 00:04:31.567
And then I was like [Vocalizes]

00:04:31.567 --> 00:04:33.334
And I was about to go like,
"She starts swinging."

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:36.467
And I go, "Hey, dude!
What's going on?"

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:38.601
-You literally -- I kept
singing -- I looked at you,

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:40.400
and I was like, "He's not
going to keep singing."

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.033
So now I'm on the teleprompter
singing your lines, right?

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:44.667
Because I don't know your lines.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:47.067
And I look over, and you're
dancing with John Mayer.

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:50.767
And I literally, at one point,
went like, "Hey, let's go!"

00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:52.167
Unbelievable.

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:54.167
-Denis, I want to talk to you
about your show, buddy.

00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:56.133
I want to talk
about "The Moodys."

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:57.267
-Yes.
-Here we go.

00:04:57.267 --> 00:05:00.267
This is -- It's a family sitcom.

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:03.701
Elizabeth Perkins, super funny.

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:05.667
You get to play hockey,
which is cool.

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:08.033
-Yeah, I get to play hockey.
So, I'll give you the setup.

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:10.634
You know, it's a limited series
every time it comes on.

00:05:10.634 --> 00:05:13.567
So, the first time we did it,
it was about family Christmas.

00:05:13.567 --> 00:05:16.100
This year, there's
a family wedding that --

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:18.734
It starts out the first
15 seconds of episode 1.

00:05:18.734 --> 00:05:20.634
You know that the wedding
didn't go well.

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:22.100
And then we flash back.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:24.601
The kids have been locked down
with us in the pandemic,

00:05:24.601 --> 00:05:27.067
like a lot of us in real life.

00:05:27.067 --> 00:05:28.901
-Yep.
-And now the pandemic's over

00:05:28.901 --> 00:05:31.167
and two of them leave,
and then they come right back.

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:33.934
So we're really getting
on each other's nerves

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:35.234
even after the pandemic,

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.000
and everybody's supposed
to be living out on their own.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.334
I think that's what
the clip's about.

00:05:38.334 --> 00:05:40.133
-Yeah. It's super funny.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:43.067
Here's Denis Leary in
the new season of "The Moodys."

00:05:43.067 --> 00:05:44.267
Take a look.

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:46.067
-Hey, look at this.

00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:48.434
All three of my adult children
living at home,

00:05:48.434 --> 00:05:51.634
eating my food,
and using my gas-powered heat.

00:05:51.634 --> 00:05:53.267
How delightful.

00:05:53.267 --> 00:05:55.601
So, right now,

00:05:55.601 --> 00:05:58.100
I'm going to go over
to the fridge

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:00.267
and get some cream.

00:06:00.267 --> 00:06:02.734
And there better be enough
left for my coffee,

00:06:02.734 --> 00:06:05.033
'cause if there isn't,
I'm going to find the culprit,

00:06:05.033 --> 00:06:09.067
and I will have two of my adult
children living at home with me.

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:11.901
Uh-oh.

00:06:11.901 --> 00:06:15.000
Oh, that's -- it's not good.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.400
Ooh, this just --

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:17.868
I don't think it's going to --

00:06:17.868 --> 00:06:19.100
Ah.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:23.334
Mm...

00:06:23.334 --> 00:06:25.367
Well, yes.

00:06:25.367 --> 00:06:26.667
We remain a family of five.

00:06:26.667 --> 00:06:27.934
-Yay.

00:06:27.934 --> 00:06:29.968
-[ Laughs ] Yeah!

00:06:29.968 --> 00:06:31.133
Denis Leary, everybody.

